  "boot_probe_deltas": "A.0 for V6-0.3 ran as a 6-probe + 6-adversarial-audit fan-out (12 agents, 0 errors). 4 of 6 probe MECHANISMS were refuted by their auditors while conclusions largely survived - consistent with the standing #verify-the-reviewer-s-MECHANISM pattern, now 4 sessions running. HEADLINE DELTA (supervisor-verified a third time by reading raw lines): V6-0.2's tier milestone banner, shipped S129 and marked DONE, PROVABLY CANNOT RENDER. drawTierBanner iterates world.effects (ui.ts:284) but hud.sync is called at main.ts:2515 while effectsRenderer.sync wipes world.effects at main.ts:2486 (effectsRenderer.ts:73); exactly one call site each, nothing between them writes world.effects. Compounding: SCORE_TIER is host-local-only (serializeEffect returns null, save.ts:1400) so even after an ordering fix it can never fire on a joining client. It passed CHECK because ui.tierBanner.test.ts pins only the pure helpers and its own docblock concedes the draw path cannot be driven headlessly. SECOND DELTA: the pre-scoped V6-0.3 plan was wrong in two places - (a) an actor id ALONE cannot answer 'am I the victim?' because BOND_SEVERED carries only {kind,tick,pos,cause} and the bond plus (in the delete case) its endpoints are removed before the emit; the cheap fix is primA.placedBy (primitive.ts:28, readonly PlayerId, immutable vs the mutable placerColor, and already used as the repo's own bond-victim derivation at creatureAI.ts:222 / creatureLifecycle.ts:207-216); (b) the cited reuse surface comboToastRenderer.ts NEVER reads world.effects - it reads synced world fields precisely because its docblock says an effects entry 'would miss the client ~5/6 of the time', so the plan cited a surface whose design point contradicts the carrier it chose. THIRD DELTA: the BACKLOG row's cause union is 4 members; the real union has SEVEN (effects.ts:136) and 'physics' passes a hardcoded asPlayerId(0) sentinel (physicsLoop.ts:170-181), so an unconditional populate would mis-attribute every overstretch sever to seat 0. FOURTH DELTA: PROTOCOL_VERSION needs NO bump (deserializeEffect is a named-field reconstruction not positional/packed, save.ts:1412-1453; parseNetMessage never descends into snapshot.effects, protocol.ts:680-697; ARC_FLASH.creatureId? is the exact shipped precedent, git-verified at commit 5a654e7) - BUT BACKLOG.md:362, marked 'do not re-litigate', says a bump IS needed for any new serialized field, which contradicts six shipped additive-optional wire fields. That is a governance ruling, not a code fact. FIFTH DELTA (process, material): NO CI job runs vitest or typecheck - grep of vitest|npm test|typecheck|check-bundle across .github/workflows/ returns ZERO hits; only deploy.yml's `npm run build` gates anything, and e2e.yml never runs on push. The per-session 'tsc 0 / vitest 1932/1932' figure has no mechanical carrier. Also package.json:13 is bare `vitest` = WATCH mode, so a PDR naming `npm test` hangs the session; run-once is `npx vitest run`. SIXTH DELTA: R15's 17-site checklist does NOT apply to an effect-variant field add (15 of 17 sites structurally N/A), so escalating to Full would buy ceremony, not coverage.",
