    {
      "id": "P1a-v06-03-banner-repair",
      "label": "V6-0.3 sub-item 1 (Commit A) - repair the V6-0.2 tier banner, which shipped dead. Split drawTierBanner into a PRE-WIPE public drainTierBanner (scan + watermark + arming) called beside drainAudioEffects, plus an in-place private animateTierBanner (countdown/alpha/visible) still inside sync. Extract captureTierBanner as a pure function so the ordering is assertable without Pixi. Add ui.drainOrder.test.ts (source-order lock, mutation-tested + behavioural order-sensitivity). Amend the V6-0.2 roadmap row off a clean DONE.",
      "status": "completed",
      "phase": "CHECK-COMPLETE",
      "tier": "Standard",
      "check_completed": true,
      "check_method": "Standard-tier CHECK on the real diff. WHAT WAS FIXED: V6-0.2's tier banner, shipped S129 and marked DONE, could never render - its SCORE_TIER scan lived in HUD.sync, called at main.ts:2515, while effectsRenderer.sync does world.effects.length = 0 at main.ts:2486 (effectsRenderer.ts:73). I verified independently that each has exactly ONE call site and that nothing between lines 2486 and 2515 writes world.effects, so the loop always iterated ZERO entries in every mode for every player. It had passed CHECK because ui.tierBanner.test.ts pins only the pure arithmetic helpers and its own docblock concedes the draw path cannot be driven headlessly - testing everything EXCEPT the broken thing produced a confident green. FIX: split rather than relocate. drainTierBanner(world) is PUBLIC and called beside drainAudioEffects BEFORE effectsRenderer.sync; it owns the PLAYING guard, the watermark including the between-matches -1 reset, and the writes (text, fill, arming tierBannerFrames). animateTierBanner(world) stays private inside sync and owns the countdown, alpha and visible. The only field both touch is the non-PLAYING zeroing of tierBannerFrames, which is idempotent. captureTierBanner() was extracted as a new exported PURE function holding the effects scan plus the backward-tick guard - extracted specifically so the ORDERING is assertable without a Pixi Application, since the absence of that seam is precisely why S129 shipped blind. hud.sync was deliberately NOT relocated, because that would have required an argument about its order-independence relative to five other renderers whereas moving the SCAN out requires no such argument. VERIFICATION - and this is the material difference from S129, which could not verify the visual at all. rAF is still paused in a hidden Browser pane, but app.ticker.update() pumps the TRUE frame callback in PRODUCTION order, which sidesteps the blocker entirely. Driving it live in a dev page: the banner went \"\"/hidden -> 'TIER 1 - 500/1500' visible with alpha 1 and the effect's cyan fill; world.effects went 1 -> 0 in that SAME frame, which PROVES the drain read the effect before the wipe rather than merely being placed earlier in the source; it HELD on the next frame with no new effect (so the animate half owns the countdown and the drain's null-capture is inert); it HID at TITLE; and it RE-ARMED on the same tick next match with fill 0xFF0066, which proves the S129 watermark-reset fix survives the split. That last check specifically rules out the PRIME-AUDIT hazard that a careless split could produce a NEW never-renders variant - the drain latching text that never animates, or the animate running against a watermark the drain never advanced. THE GUARD WAS MUTATION-TESTED, not merely observed to pass: moving hud.drainTierBanner below the wipe makes ui.drainOrder.test.ts fail (1 failed / 8 passed), and reverting restores 9/9. A guard that only ever passes proves nothing. The suite also pins dedupe-by-tick, newest-tier-wins across a multi-tick drained batch, mixed-kind arrays, and watermark reset on a no-crossing frame. NUMBERS: tsc -b --noEmit exit 0 - npx vitest run 1941/1941 across 128 files (+9 tests, +1 file; baseline 1932/1932 across 127 was RE-RUN this session rather than inherited from the handoff) - npm run build exit 0, bundle 642.6/750 KiB with the delta MEASURED at +218 B against the 642.3 KiB baseline, 107.4 KiB headroom. Commit message content grep-verified after the fact (the backtick command-substitution trap has bitten 3x, so the message was passed via -F from a file and then checked on disk). LIMITS STATED, NOT BURIED: (1) pixel output is NOT obtainable - a hidden pane's GL context produces no frames, so renderer.extract() returns a blank raster, though it measures 271x28 with real glyph metrics and reports fill 0x00FFFF, so the glyphs demonstrably exist. Placement and legibility remain the owner's eye and that is the playtest checkpoint this commit deliberately ends on. (2) STILL SOLO/BOTS ONLY: SCORE_TIER is host-local (serializeEffect returns null, save.ts:1400), so a 1v1 JOINER still never sees the banner; putting the kind on the wire would be a new serialized literal in the S110 'WALK' bump class, so it is a LOGGED carry-forward rather than a silent gap. (3) NOT PUSHED - the gh token is still invalid, so this is now the 16th unpushed commit and no CI or e2e lane can be dispatched; there is in any case no CI job that runs vitest or typecheck at all, which is the structural reason this defect could ship green in the first place and is now P2.",
