      "label": "CI carrier - make a red test block a master-push deploy. A.0 STATE FINDING corrects the owner's ruling: the recorded claim 'NO CI job runs vitest OR typecheck' is HALF WRONG. package.json's build is 'tsc -b && vite build && check-bundle-size', so npm run build ALREADY runs tsc -b and already enforces the bundle cap - a type error already fails the deploy today, transitively. vitest is the genuine gap. Scope: gating 'npx vitest run' (NEVER 'npm test' - that script is bare vitest = watch mode and would hang the runner to its ceiling), an EXPLICIT 'npm run typecheck' step so the existing gate stops being invisible and fast-fails with the real reason, and timeout-minutes on both jobs (deploy.yml sets none today, so it inherits the 6-HOUR default). Steps go inside the existing build job before npm run build, reusing its npm ci. deploy.yml only.",
