      "check_method": "Micro-tier CHECK on a workflow file, which cannot be exercised: the gh token has no write auth, so deploy.yml has NOT run since the gate was added. Verification is static BY NECESSITY and is recorded as such rather than implying a green CI run. (1) A.0 STATE PROBE THAT CORRECTED THE OWNER'S RULING (Rule 21): the ruling rested on the recorded claim 'NO CI job runs vitest OR typecheck - zero hits across .github/workflows/'. The grep is accurate and its conclusion is HALF FALSE - package.json defines build as 'tsc -b && vite build && node scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs', so npm run build has ALWAYS run tsc -b and always enforced the bundle cap. A type error has been failing this deploy all along, transitively; vitest was the only real gap. Corrected in the amended PDR, in LOCKED_DECISIONS.md (which had repeated the claim earlier in THIS session), and in the workflow itself. (2) YAML parsed with a real parser (not regex): both jobs present, steps in order npm ci -> npm run typecheck -> npx vitest run -> npm run build, timeout-minutes 15/10. (3) NEW GUARD src/ci.deployGate.test.ts, 6 tests, MUTATION-TESTED: swapping 'npx vitest run' for 'npm test' fails it (verified, reverted). The guard asserts on the EXTRACTED run: commands, not on file text, because deploy.yml deliberately mentions 'npm test' in the warning comment that prevents the mistake - a substring check would have failed on its own documentation. It also pins that the paths filter still includes src/**, since a perfect gate behind a filter that excludes source would never fire. (4) tsc 0; vitest 1970/1970 (130 files, +6). Bundle unchanged - no src/ runtime code touched. (5) HONEST LIMITS NAMED IN-FILE: a timeout kill still concludes 'cancelled' not 'failure' (no email, no artifacts), and vitest has no global-suite-timeout flag to place below the job timeout the way PW_GLOBAL_TIMEOUT_MIN sits below Playwright's - so this bounds the WASTE without closing the silent-signal class. package.json