    {
      "id": "P3-toast-backing-plate",
      "label": "Centre-column backing plate for the two V6-0.3 read-me surfaces. The S131 playtest showed the tier banner (glyph band y 34-59) and the sever toast (y 228-249) both rendering over live world geometry - spawner rings and structures pass behind the glyphs. Text draws on top so it stays readable, but it is avoidable noise on the two lines that exist to be READ. Add a dark semi-transparent plate behind each, on the shipped betaBadgePlate precedent (main.ts:540). Plate alpha must be driven by the SAME countdown/container alpha as its text so the two appear and fade as one object, and must be invisible whenever the text is - a plate outliving its text is a black rectangle on the board. NO repositioning: the owner ruled PASS on placement; this is legibility only.",
