    "NEW S130 (PRIME-AUDIT R-C, open by construction): the drain-order source lock protects only the consumers named in its allowlist. Nothing stops a future session adding an unlisted world.effects reader AFTER the wipe at main.ts:2486. The defect CLASS is mitigated for known consumers and OPEN for new ones.",
    "NEW S130 (PRIME-AUDIT R-B, watch first in the playtest): physics-cause toast spam. No Council leg addressed frequency. Per-frame coalescing bounds it to one toast per frame, but under 'Overwrite = restart' a chronically rubber-banding structure holds a persistent OVERSTRETCHED toast. Cheapest mitigation is dropping the physics row entirely - it is the one row with no attribution to make.",
