  "council_result": "S131 CHECK — TRIUMVIRATE, run at the owner's explicit request ('go'). Three legs returned; the panel was deliberately split by STRENGTH rather than giving all three the same diff: internal agents that can READ the repo took code-level review (this project's documented failure mode is reviewers filing criticals against symbols that do not exist), while the external models took design-level adversarial reasoning with the decision-dense logic inline. RALPH (4 lenses + a refutation pass per finding, 10 agents, 0 errors): 6 raised, 4 CONFIRMED, 2 REFUTED. Every confirmation was empirical — the refuters RAN each mutation instead of arguing it. All 4 confirmed findings were guards written THIS SESSION that would pass while the thing they name was broken: (i) the deserialize half of the wire was unasserted, so deleting the actor/victim pass-through left 1981/1981 green and a joiner would get NO toast at all; (ii) the plate test never referenced the plate, so deleting both plate assignments left P3's banner half dead and green; (iii) the drain-order guard — the one that exists solely to prevent the V6-0.2 defect — used String.indexOf with no comment stripping, and main.ts already carried the consumer name in a comment one `(world)` token from blinding it, demonstrated live with the defect active and the full suite green; (iv) the CI guard pinned flat file order, not the job graph, so moving the gates into a sibling job (or deleting `needs:`) passed every assertion while deploy stopped waiting on the tests. All four fixed and re-mutation-verified (commit 05ea263). GROK-ANALYST (grok-4.20-0309-reasoning): 5 findings, 2 actionable and fixed in 2fd05b8 — the tolerant-default arm was asserting the 'player' mechanism, so a mixed creature+drone batch read as a direct hostile sever; and severActor's deny-list was replaced by an exhaustive switch over the six-member ACTION union with a `never` guard (verified: deleting a case now fails tsc with TS2322). Its other 3 (backwards-tick toast loss, alpha 0 on the capture frame, fade-to-0.03 boundary) were assessed and declined with reasons recorded in the commit message. GEMINI-AUDITOR (gemini-3.1-pro-preview): TIMED OUT at 120s on the first, 3-part brief; retried narrow and returned. Independently CONFIRMED the no-PROTOCOL_VERSION-bump claim in both skew directions and on the localStorage save path, on the grounds that deserialize maps named fields with no spread and JSON.stringify drops undefined keys. Its only observation was that an old client parses then discards the two fields. NET: the CHECK found nothing broken for users today — all 6 actioned findings were future-regression gaps — but it found that 4 of my own new guards were vacuous, which is exactly the class of defect that shipped V6-0.2 dead.",
  "prime_audit_result": "PRIME-AUDIT on the S131 CHECK itself. WHAT WAS RUBBER-STAMPED: nothing silently — the two reducer/lifecycle lenses returned ZERO findings, and rather than treat that as a pass I note it is consistent with those surfaces having been the ones I derived most carefully from raw lines. WHAT SURVIVED CONSENSUS THAT SHOULD NOT: my own docblock's stated mechanism for bomb-suppression clause (b). A reviewer tried to prove the clause redundant and FAILED — the clause is needed — but its refutation established that my stated reason was wrong (within one match the rainbow shuffle applies one bijection to both player.color and placerColor and PRESERVES the correspondence; divergence needs the shuffle plus the next match's static re-seating, because colour is never reset and START_GAME leaves a seated player in place). Correct conclusion, wrong mechanism — the #verify-the-reviewer-s-MECHANISM pattern, now 5 sessions running, this time applied to my OWN comment. Corrected in code. REVIEWER PRECISION, AUDITED BOTH WAYS: 3 of 6 findings cited a line 20-40 lines off target, and one REFUTED finding was refuted PRIMARILY on a wrong-line citation — so the anti-fabrication posture earned its keep in both directions. No finding named a nonexistent symbol; the refuters existence-checked first, as instructed. One refuter also caught a factual error INSIDE a finding it confirmed (the claimed toast degradation was wrong; the real behaviour is no toast at all) and confirmed anyway because the error understated the harm — that is the right call. RUNTIME-VERIFIABILITY: the CI carrier remains STATIC-ONLY by necessity (no write auth, so deploy.yml has never run with its gate). Everything else in the session was verified with real pixels through genuine emitters, not static parse. WHAT REMAINS UNVERIFIED AND IS NOT BEING PRETENDED OTHERWISE: (a) deploy.yml has not executed once; (b) the networked ~1/6 sever-toast delivery path has no e2e coverage and the e2e lane has not run since S127; (c) the tick-driven toast hold is untested against a genuinely frozen sim clock while frames render. All three are carry-forwards, not claims.",
  "analyze_completed": true,
