      "what_to_change": [
        "MUTATION-TEST EVERY NEW ASSERTION, not just the ones that look load-bearing. I mutation-tested 3 guards and shipped 4 untested ones; the panel broke all 4. There is no reliable intuition for which assertion is vacuous — only deletion tells you.",
        "SWEEP FOR THE CLASS, not the instance. I fixed 'assert on extracted commands, not raw file text' in the CI guard and left the identical indexOf-matches-comments hole in the drain-order guard the same hour. When a class of bug is found, grep for its siblings immediately.",
        "READ THE REASONING OF REFUTED FINDINGS. The most valuable correction of the session came from a finding that was REFUTED — the refutation proved my conclusion right and my stated mechanism wrong.",
        "TREAT 'FULLY SPECCED, DO NOT RE-DERIVE' as covering the DECISION, never the external state it rests on. Rule 21 still applies to a plan's factual anchors: 3 of this plan's failed."
